summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Follow up of chronic problems.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Carolyn Thompson is a 49-year-old female who presents today for the follow up of her chronic problems.

The patient reports that her osteoarthritis has been flaring up lately. She states that she has been sitting at her desk more at work and she is not sure if this has increased flare ups of her elbows. She reports that her right elbow hurts more than her left. She denies other joint pain. She notes that she feels a little bit of numbness in her hands when typing for long periods of time and she shakes her arms to relieve this sensation.

The patient reports that she had a flare of gout 3 months ago with inflammation of her toe. She reports that the medication that I gave her controlled this and she has not seen a flare up since.

The patient reports that her psoriasis is under control and she has not had any major problems with this.

The patient reports that she has been using clobetasol for her scalp and this has been doing well.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Musculoskeletal: Reports right elbow pain. Denies other joint pain.
• Neurological: Endorses numbness in her hands when typing for long periods of time.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

• Neck: No cervical lymphadenopathy.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.
• Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs, gallops, or rubs. No extra heart sounds.
• Musculoskeletal: Right elbow has some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. Tenderness and effusion present over the olecranon. Pain with palpation of the olecranon bursa, pain with pronation and supination. Pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. Bilateral upper extremity strength is 5/5. Normal gait.

RESULTS

Autoimmune panel is within normal limits. Uric acid is within normal limits. ESR is within normal limits.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Carolyn Thompson is a 49-year-old female who presents today for the follow up of her chronic problems.

Gout.
• Medical Reasoning: She reports that she had a flare of gout 3 months ago with inflammation of her toe. She reports that the medication that I gave her controlled this and she has not seen a flare up since.
• Medical Treatment: Continue colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare ups of gout.

Osteoarthritis.
• Medical Reasoning: She reports that she has been sitting at her desk more at work and she is not sure if this has increased flare ups of her elbows.
• Medical Treatment: Order right elbow x-ray. Prescription for meloxicam 15 mg once a day.

Psoriasis.
• Medical Reasoning: She reports that she has been using clobetasol for her scalp and this has been doing well.
• Medical Treatment: Continue clobetasol.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

I would like to see the results of the x-ray before we refer her for physical therapy. }}<|eot_id|>
