The patient reports that her blood sugars have been up and down. She states that her blood sugar levels have been elevated and that her diet has been poor lately. She notes that she has been snacking a lot at work, as she recently started a new job at a bakery. She denies any other symptoms.

The patient reports that her blood pressure has been normal. She denies any concerns for self-harm. She states that she has been sleeping well and getting 8 hours of sleep per night.

