Rebecca Thomas is a 27-year-old female who presents today for the evaluation of right knee pain. She reports that last week and over the course of the month she has been swimming regularly. She states that she was able to do 10 laps without any pain initially but after a couple of laps, she starts to feel pain in her right knee. She denies any injury. She states that she only swims breaststroke. She denies any pain with walking or standing. She reports that she has a history of carpal tunnel syndrome, which she had surgery for a couple of years ago. She also has a history of chronic back pain and depression. She states that she has been doing well with her back pain. She denies any pain that radiates down her legs. She denies any suicidal or homicidal ideations. She states that she has been doing well with her depression medication and therapy. She denies any sleep issues. She denies any appetite issues. She denies any joint swelling. She reports that she has a full range of motion in her wrist. She denies any pain with range of motion of her knee. She reports pain with patellar inhibition.
