summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Full spectrum STD testing.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Ross is a 20 year old female who presents for full spectrum STD testing. She states she is having symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. The patient states the right side of her vagina is starting to become painful. She denies fevers or chills. She reports that she recently learned that her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people and she wants to be evaluated for all STDs.

Ms. Ross states that she started noticing some weird discharge last week. She states the discharge smells different, it's not the same color or consistency as it usually is. She states that part did not phase her until she noticed that the right side of her vagina was hurting. She states it is just sore, but that has not gone away.

Ms. Ross states she has been dating her partner for 3 years. She states that she thinks he started cheating on her about 3 months ago.

The patient states she had an abnormal Pap smear in the past, but she has not had one since she was 20. She states she had her last Pap smear about 6 months ago, which was normal.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fevers or chills.
Genitourinary: Reports vaginal discharge, pain, and odor.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Examination of the Genitourinary system: External female genitalia normal. No external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge, with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted.

RESULTS

Swabs were done for STD testing.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

The patient is a 20-year-old female who presents for full spectrum STD testing. She is a high risk patient due to an abnormal Pap smear in the past and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners for some period of time.

The patient's symptoms are most likely due to a sexually transmitted infection. I have recommended that we perform STD testing.

Patient will undergo gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, and syphilis, HIV and hepatitis C testing today.

Patient will be contacted if anything is abnormal. She will be advised to follow up with us in 3 days for results if she does not hear from us.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.
