The patient states that she has not had any fever with the pain. She reports that she has been doing well with her diabetes and her blood sugars have been under control. She is currently taking metformin 500 mg once a day. She notes that she has not had any asthma attacks recently and she has been taking Flovent twice a day and albuterol as needed for wheezing.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fevers.
• Gastrointestinal: Reports abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting.
• Respiratory: End-expiratory wheezes.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

• Cardiovascular: Grade 3/6 systolic ejection murmur.
• Respiratory: End-expiratory wheezes, very faint.
• Gastrointestinal: Mild tenderness in the epigastrium. Otherwise soft, no tenderness in the right lower quadrant. No significant tenderness in the right upper quadrant.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Acute gastritis.
- Medical Reasoning: The patient presents with abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. She has a history of alcohol abuse and increased coffee intake.
- Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient to cut back on alcohol and caffeine.
- Medical Treatment: I am going to prescribe her Zantac twice a day.
- Additional Testing: I am going to check a urinalysis, urine pregnancy test, CBC, and CMP.

2. Diabetes type 2.
- Medical Reasoning: The patient has been doing well with her diabetes. Her blood sugars have been under control.
- Medical Treatment: I am going to increase her metformin to 1000 mg in the morning and 500 mg in the evening.

3. Asthma.
- Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well with Flovent. She has not had any asthma attacks recently.
- Medical Treatment: I advised her to continue Flovent daily and use albuterol as needed.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with me in 4 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
